1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,680
Hello again!

2
00:00:00,680 --> 00:00:04,640
Last time, we got completely stuck.

3
00:00:04,640 --> 00:00:07,580
Do you remember what saved us?

4
00:00:07,580 --> 00:00:10,280
The big friend trick!

5
00:00:10,280 --> 00:00:14,280
Take away the friend, and carry to the tens rod.

6
00:00:14,280 --> 00:00:18,560
This video is all about big friend adding.

7
00:00:18,560 --> 00:00:21,080
Today we learn all five.

8
00:00:21,080 --> 00:00:22,280
Ready?

9
00:00:22,280 --> 00:00:23,440
Let us go.

10
00:00:23,440 --> 00:00:27,120
First, let us meet them all.

11
00:00:27,120 --> 00:00:30,920
Every number that needs a big friend has one.

12
00:00:30,920 --> 00:00:34,560
Five pairs that make ten together.

13
00:00:34,560 --> 00:00:35,680
Look.

14
00:00:35,680 --> 00:00:37,460
One and nine.

15
00:00:37,460 --> 00:00:40,040
One and nine make ten.

16
00:00:40,040 --> 00:00:41,680
So they are friends.

17
00:00:41,680 --> 00:00:45,180
Two and eight make ten as well.

18
00:00:45,180 --> 00:00:48,180
Three and seven make ten.

19
00:00:48,180 --> 00:00:51,660
Four and six make ten.

20
00:00:51,660 --> 00:00:54,220
And five and...

21
00:00:54,220 --> 00:00:55,060
five!

22
00:00:55,060 --> 00:00:58,380
A number can be its own friend.

23
00:00:58,380 --> 00:01:00,920
Now you tell me.

24
00:01:00,920 --> 00:01:02,580
Who is two's friend?

25
00:01:02,580 --> 00:01:05,080
Eight!

26
00:01:05,080 --> 00:01:06,180
Well done.

27
00:01:06,180 --> 00:01:08,740
And six's friend?

28
00:01:08,740 --> 00:01:10,880
Four!

29
00:01:10,880 --> 00:01:12,220
You have got it.

30
00:01:12,220 --> 00:01:14,840
So four's friend is six.

31
00:01:15,580 --> 00:01:17,840
And six's friend is four.

32
00:01:17,840 --> 00:01:21,120
Now, careful here.

33
00:01:21,120 --> 00:01:23,000
This part is important.

34
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:26,820
We do not always need the big friend.

35
00:01:26,820 --> 00:01:30,400
Always look at the whole rod first.

36
00:01:30,400 --> 00:01:34,200
If there is still room, just push the beads.

37
00:01:34,200 --> 00:01:35,420
Watch.

38
00:01:35,420 --> 00:01:37,620
Six plus two.

39
00:01:37,620 --> 00:01:42,580
Push one lower bead up, then the upper bead down.

40
00:01:42,580 --> 00:01:44,840
That makes six.

41
00:01:44,840 --> 00:01:48,120
Now push two more lower beads.

42
00:01:48,120 --> 00:01:49,360
Done!

43
00:01:49,360 --> 00:01:51,080
That was easy.

44
00:01:51,080 --> 00:01:52,540
No trick at all.

45
00:01:52,540 --> 00:01:54,700
The rod still had room.

46
00:01:54,700 --> 00:01:58,500
But do you remember nine plus one?

47
00:01:59,460 --> 00:02:01,460
We pushed, and pushed...

48
00:02:01,460 --> 00:02:03,940
and there was nothing left.

49
00:02:03,940 --> 00:02:07,440
Not one bead, anywhere on the rod.

50
00:02:07,440 --> 00:02:11,200
And that is when we call a big friend.

51
00:02:11,200 --> 00:02:16,300
Now, you already met three of these friends last time.

52
00:02:16,300 --> 00:02:18,700
Nine and one.

53
00:02:18,700 --> 00:02:20,660
Eight and two.

54
00:02:20,660 --> 00:02:22,920
Seven and three.

55
00:02:22,920 --> 00:02:27,520
Take away the friend, then carry to the tens rod.

56
00:02:27,520 --> 00:02:31,060
Every one of those made ten.

57
00:02:31,900 --> 00:02:33,880
And here is something neat.

58
00:02:33,880 --> 00:02:36,500
It works flipped around too.

59
00:02:36,500 --> 00:02:39,100
Two and eight.

60
00:02:39,100 --> 00:02:41,700
Make two on your abacus.

61
00:02:41,700 --> 00:02:44,000
Just two lower beads.

62
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:50,420
Eight's friend is two — and that is exactly what is already there.

63
00:02:50,420 --> 00:02:55,720
Take away two, then carry one bead to the tens rod.

64
00:02:55,720 --> 00:02:58,780
Two plus eight is ten.

65
00:02:58,780 --> 00:03:02,060
Same trick, just flipped.

66
00:03:02,060 --> 00:03:06,400
So today, let us learn the last two.

67
00:03:06,400 --> 00:03:09,480
Four's friend is six.

68
00:03:09,480 --> 00:03:12,100
Let us make six.

69
00:03:12,100 --> 00:03:16,760
Push one lower bead up, then the upper bead down.

70
00:03:16,760 --> 00:03:20,280
Now we want to add four.

71
00:03:20,280 --> 00:03:22,560
Remember our rule.

72
00:03:22,560 --> 00:03:28,720
The ones rod goes first, and lower beads move before the upper bead.

73
00:03:28,720 --> 00:03:31,360
So take away six.

74
00:03:31,360 --> 00:03:36,700
Down comes one lower bead, then up goes the upper bead.

75
00:03:36,700 --> 00:03:40,300
Now the ones rod shows zero.

76
00:03:40,300 --> 00:03:41,580
Oh!

77
00:03:41,580 --> 00:03:43,020
Zero already?

78
00:03:43,020 --> 00:03:44,940
Do not worry.

79
00:03:44,940 --> 00:03:46,960
Watch what happens next.

80
00:03:46,960 --> 00:03:50,460
Now the tens rod gets its turn.

81
00:03:50,460 --> 00:03:52,700
Carry one bead.

82
00:03:53,260 --> 00:03:54,400
And there it is.

83
00:03:54,400 --> 00:03:55,140
Ten!

84
00:03:55,140 --> 00:03:58,180
Six plus four is ten.

85
00:03:58,180 --> 00:04:02,360
We wanted four more, and we got it.

86
00:04:02,360 --> 00:04:04,540
Enjoying this?

87
00:04:04,540 --> 00:04:08,300
Give this video a like, and subscribe for more.

88
00:04:08,300 --> 00:04:11,020
Now stop and look.

89
00:04:11,020 --> 00:04:12,980
Did you see it?

90
00:04:12,980 --> 00:04:17,680
Every single time, we did the same two things.

91
00:04:17,680 --> 00:04:21,720
Take away the friend, on the ones rod first.

92
00:04:21,720 --> 00:04:25,240
Then carry one bead to the tens rod.

93
00:04:25,240 --> 00:04:26,940
That is all.

94
00:04:26,940 --> 00:04:29,000
The friend changes.

95
00:04:29,000 --> 00:04:31,560
But ten never does.

96
00:04:31,560 --> 00:04:34,420
Here is something neat.

97
00:04:34,420 --> 00:04:38,500
It works the other way round too.

98
00:04:38,500 --> 00:04:40,680
Let us flip it.

99
00:04:40,680 --> 00:04:42,020
Four plus six.

100
00:04:42,020 --> 00:04:45,140
Make four on your abacus.

101
00:04:45,140 --> 00:04:47,440
Just four lower beads.

102
00:04:47,440 --> 00:04:55,400
Six's friend is four — and look, that is exactly what is already there.

103
00:04:55,400 --> 00:05:01,060
So take away four, then carry one bead to the tens rod.

104
00:05:02,160 --> 00:05:04,540
Four plus six is ten.

105
00:05:04,540 --> 00:05:06,800
Same trick.

106
00:05:06,800 --> 00:05:08,480
Just flipped around.

107
00:05:08,480 --> 00:05:11,000
Now it is your turn.

108
00:05:11,000 --> 00:05:12,440
All on your own.

109
00:05:12,440 --> 00:05:15,520
Make five on your abacus.

110
00:05:15,520 --> 00:05:17,600
Just the upper bead.

111
00:05:17,600 --> 00:05:20,300
Then add five.

112
00:05:20,300 --> 00:05:21,620
Think.

113
00:05:21,620 --> 00:05:23,780
What is five's friend?

114
00:05:23,780 --> 00:05:25,940
Five!

115
00:05:25,940 --> 00:05:29,440
A number really can be its own friend.

116
00:05:29,440 --> 00:05:34,640
Take it away, then carry one bead to the tens rod.

117
00:05:34,640 --> 00:05:37,660
What number is showing now?

118
00:05:39,600 --> 00:05:41,720
Five plus five is ten.

119
00:05:41,720 --> 00:05:43,620
Did you get it?

120
00:05:43,620 --> 00:05:44,860
Well done!

121
00:05:44,860 --> 00:05:49,600
That was the fifth friend, and you did it by yourself.

122
00:05:50,420 --> 00:05:54,280
So now you know all five big friends for adding.

123
00:05:54,280 --> 00:05:59,220
That is a real abacus formula, and it is yours.

124
00:06:00,040 --> 00:06:03,160
Try them at home on your own abacus.

125
00:06:03,160 --> 00:06:08,780
Search for abacus kids on the Apple App Store or Google Play.

126
00:06:09,360 --> 00:06:10,620
Download it free.

127
00:06:10,620 --> 00:06:15,720
Next time, we will learn the big friends for taking away.

128
00:06:15,720 --> 00:06:17,780
See you next time!
